<title>HONG KONG: Wharf interim net falls 56.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Wharf interim net falls 56.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   59.0	  vs 138.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    26.0	  vs 24.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  102.70 gain vs 1,945.9 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    1,302.40    vs 3,002.4</p>
<p>    Turnover		     3,669.10    vs 3,309.2</p>
<p>    Company name		 Wharf (Holdings) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  October 22-28</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   November 4</p>
<p>NOTE - Wharf is a holding company for property, hotel, transport and warehousing businesses.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$102.70 million on sale of certain investment properties and Omni Hotels interest in the United States. Exceptional gain last year was on sale of the group's interest in a subsidiary listed in Singapore.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
